---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Copyright & Takedown Policy" description="How copyright holders can report a WasmStore listing and request review or removal of linked game content." path="/copyright">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">RIGHTS & RESPONSIBLE CURATION</div><h1>Copyright &amp; <span class="gradient-text">takedowns</span></h1><p>How to request a review of a listing, attribution, or linked material.</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <p>WasmStore is an independent directory that helps visitors discover browser-playable games and community projects. Many entries link to third-party demos, repositories, or external services; a listing does not mean WasmStore owns or hosts the underlying game or assets.</p>
    <h2>Submit a request</h2>
    <p>If you are a rights holder or an authorized representative and believe a WasmStore page infringes your rights, please use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> and select the copyright / takedown topic. Include enough detail for us to identify and review the material.</p>
    <h2>Information to include</h2>
    <ul><li>Your name and reliable contact details, and the rights holder you represent if applicable.</li><li>The exact WasmStore page URL(s) you want reviewed.</li><li>The copyrighted work or trademark at issue and an explanation of the concern.</li><li>The URL of the original or allegedly infringing material, if available.</li><li>A statement that you believe in good faith the reported use is not authorized and that the information you provide is accurate.</li></ul>
    <h2>Review process</h2>
    <p>We will review the information and may remove or amend a listing, disable a link, or request clarification. Where material is hosted by a third party, you may also need to contact that provider directly. A request does not guarantee a particular outcome.</p>
    <h2>Contact and limitations</h2>
    <p>Start at the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. The site's owner must configure and monitor the contact channel before this process can be considered operational. This page is general information, not legal advice, and does not replace any formal notice required by applicable law.</p>
    <p>For the site's independent status, see the <a href="/non-affiliation">Non-affiliation notice</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
